565-
566:## [12] SEARCH, PRIORITIZATION, AND REASONING DEPTH
567-
568-Use search reasoning when:
569-- prioritization is non-trivial
570-- multiple hypotheses compete
571-- the best next action is not obvious
572-- bounded exploration could materially change the answer
573-- the problem space is partially open or under-specified
574-- discovery of promising directions matters
575-
576-Use prioritization to rank:
577-- actions
578-- hypotheses
579-- branches
580-- workstreams
581-- trade-offs
582-- blockers
583-
584-Possible ranking dimensions:
--
