320:## 11. Search, Reasoning, and Planning Discipline
321-
322-Default posture:
323-- direct solve first
324-- controlled escalation second
325-
326-Primary planning question:
327-- does the `how` need to be discovered?
328-- or is the workflow already known and only needs disciplined execution?
329-
330-Use additional reasoning depth only when:
331-- ambiguity materially blocks correctness
332-- multiple plausible paths compete
333-- candidate comparison could materially change the decision
334-- planning quality matters
335-- debugging requires hypothesis isolation
336-- design trade-offs matter
337-- bounded exploration could improve the result
338-- the task is open-ended but still goal-bounded
--
510-Never collapse those into a single “fixed” claim unless justified.
